From bf165c9ad7e0683ebbeef6cddbc57f35cb3768a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneplus6t port <none@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:12:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sdm845: warm-reset the PMIC on every restart

msm-poweroff reads qcom,force-warm-reboot from the pshold restart node
and, when present, takes the PON_POWER_OFF_WARM_RESET path on every
restart rather than only on panic/dload. A warm reset keeps DDR
contents, so the ramoops region (0x400000@0xac300000, per
sdm845_enchilada_soc.dtsi and confirmed live on LineageOS: "ramoops:
attached 0x400000@0xac300000") survives into the next boot and
/sys/fs/pstore carries the previous boot's console.

Without it, a kernel that dies before userspace goes through a cold
reset and the log is gone: the first Halium boot on LineageOS 20's
vendor died ~12 s after handoff, and pstore on the following boot was
empty. This is the only console this device has -- the UART is on
unpopulated test points under the shield cans and OnePlus did not enable
USB-C debug accessory mode -- so it is not optional for bring-up.

Patch 0003 adds a runtime module parameter for the same PMIC decision;
that only helps once userspace exists to set it. This DT property is the
build-time form for the boots where nothing does.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
index 8bc98dd5654c..883260feb978 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi
@@ -861,6 +861,7 @@
 		reg = <0xC264000 0x4>,
 		      <0x1fd3000 0x4>;
 		reg-names = "pshold-base", "tcsr-boot-misc-detect";
+		qcom,force-warm-reboot;
 	};
 
 	aop-msg-client {
